# Producer checkouts cloned to reproduce the coherence gates locally.
# `skill-registry-coherence.yml` clones FS.GG.SDD / FS.GG.Rendering / FS.GG.Game into `.repos/`
# and runs `fsgg-skill-registry-check --repos-root .repos`. That is the only way to run the gate
# outside CI, so every registry reconcile does it — and in a fresh item worktree a `git add -A`
# would otherwise stage three full repository clones.
.repos/

# Python bytecode from the checker scripts (`check-feed-coherence.py` et al. import `fsgg_feed`,
# so merely RUNNING a gate writes these). One was committed this way in ac10a61 — a registry
# release PR that swept it in — and it then showed as modified in every worker's tree.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# .NET build output (FS.GG.Coord.Core, ADR-0034 Phase 1; and scripts/NewSddWorkspace).
# `.repos/` and `__pycache__` are already handled above (#443) — same rule: a generated artifact is
# never authored, so it is never in a `Paths:` touch-set and never in a commit.
bin/
obj/

# Local coordination session telemetry is a disposable projection, not an authority. Durable host
# reasoning belongs in the issue/PR comment that records the decision (including structured
# delivery-route and review receipts); board fields remain projections of those records.
.fsgg/coord-report/
# M5: bulky execution output belongs in immutable CI artifacts. Existing tracked
# files remain tracked until their recoverable M6 migration; this prevents new copies.
**/test-results/
TestResults/
